at the foot of the tianshan mountains  kyrgyz farmers guide their horses  towards fields  where the snow is less deep so they can  graze  horses from this region were fought over  and prized by nomad clans invading  armies  and russian settlers for centuries  to farmers like bucket chokyov they are  a source of wealth cultural identity  and national  the pride is the kirkey's man's right  hand we are originally normal  we discovered new places riding horses  like this we drink their milk and eat  their meat  horses mean so much for our culture  each of these animals is worth around  two thousand dollars protecting them  from mountain predators can be a  challenge  especially at this time of year  this winter has been very bad for  attacks by wolves  four horses in the village have been  killed so far  for the farmer the hardy indigenous  breeds of horses remain fundamental to  their working lives but they also breed  them  with animals from europe and one of the  reasons is a desire for victory  in the national sport the game of ulak  tartish demands a horse not only be  strong  riders wrestle over a goat carcass they  have to drop the animal into a score  zone to win  points kinan sadira kulov has been  competing for four years  his horse polkovnik meaning colonel in  english  is a kyrgyz european mixed breed  we need them to be agile and fast  there's a lot of horses with physical  ability but they get scared  they also can't be too tall because we  need to bend them down and grab the good  carcass  russian settlers were the first to mix  kyrgyz with european breeds when they  came to this region in the mid 19th  century  there is now increasing interest among  stud farm owners like  bechter shabnakov to breed pure european  horses specifically for racing  he breeds imported english animals which  cost from around fifty thousand dollars  to transport from the uk  the difficulties of raising pure foreign  breeds is you need better quality  pasture and vitamins  they're not used to harsh winters it's  much more challenging and expensive  horses are a way of life in this  mountainous region of central asia  for bucket and his fellow herders they  mean more  than money and prestige  al jazeera northern kyrgyzstan
 

